summary_en.experiments:
On bug localization and code generation benchmarks, CodeComp consistently outperforms attention-only KV compression baselines (e.g., SnapKV, ParallelComp) under equal KV memory budgets. Motivation experiments show:
- Strong misalignment between attention importance and CPG-based structural importance (top-20% chunk Jaccard ≈ 0.0944);
- Attention-only compression prunes a substantial fraction of structurally critical tokens across categories;
- Structure-aware selection retains more critical tokens across all categories and recovers most full-context accuracy under aggressive compression; patch generation quality can match uncompressed full-context inference (as stated in the abstract).
